# Slice 333: the descriptor f2, without a body, merged into f1 by the general rules of Structure (the author 2026-11-08):
# the parts of the Structure of fn are composed -- args takes f2's default of b (7) into f1's formal b, return takes f2's
# word -- and the code stays f1's. R is that Structure, data, held by the place `@: R merge(f1; f2)`; `fn: g R` makes the
# function g of it: g(1) reads b from the new signature (17) where f1(1) reads f1's (12). f1 and f2 stay as written.
# M11 5v: ordered own data first constructs R, then gives it to fn. The
# final reference exposes the complete result after both numeric calls.
fn: f1 (int: a; int: b 2) int
    return: a * 10 + b
fn: f2 (int: b 7) int
int: descriptor_parts length(f2)
sub: main () (
    @: R merge(f1; f2)
    fn: g R
    int: r1 0
    int: r2 0
)
    r1 := f1(1)
    r2 := g(1)
main()
int: r1 main\data\r1
int: r2 main\data\r2
@: observed_R main\data\R
